<title>CHINA: U.S., China reach agreement on table grape exports.</title>
<headline>U.S., China reach agreement on table grape exports.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>China and the United States on Monday signed a protocol allowing for the legal export of California table grapes to China for the first time, a U.S. embassy official in Beijing said.</p>
<p>The official said he was unable to estimate the value of the grape exports that would result, but said he believed it would be substantial.</p>
<p>California table grapes are currently available in many of China's cities, but are imported illegally, usually through Hong Kong.</p>
<p>The official said agreement had been reached for table grapes from four California counties -- Fresno, Tulare, Kern and Madera -- to be exported to China.</p>
</text>
